{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00859",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.63,
      "end_seconds": 12.75,
      "duration_seconds": 12.12,
      "text": "Hiya, Kelly, I'm Dawn, the nurse. I'll weigh you and take your blood pressure first, then the doctor will go through your blood test. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.21,
      "end_seconds": 22.37,
      "duration_seconds": 8.16,
      "text": "Lovely. Oh, I've got so much to tell you, doctor, I've been reading all about it. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 45.03,
      "end_seconds": 51.66,
      "duration_seconds": 6.63,
      "text": "Weight 63 kilos, blood pressure 114 over 70, pulse 68, temperature 36.5."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 53.07,
      "end_seconds": 62.08,
      "duration_seconds": 9.01,
      "text": "Hello, Kelly. It's your coeliac follow-up. You've been on the gluten-free diet for six months now. How's it going?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.87,
      "end_seconds": 78.23,
      "duration_seconds": 13.36,
      "text": "Brilliant, honestly, once I got the hang of it. I've learned to read every label. I've been to a few restaurants. And my tummy's so much better. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 79.17,
      "end_seconds": 85.49,
      "duration_seconds": 6.32,
      "text": "And the bloating, and the loose stools you had before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 87.43,
      "end_seconds": 97.37,
      "duration_seconds": 9.94,
      "text": "Gone. Well, almost. I haven't had a bad day in two months. No diarrhoea at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.33,
      "end_seconds": 104.52,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "Any tummy pain, or other symptoms? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 106.91,
      "end_seconds": 112.2,
      "duration_seconds": 5.29,
      "text": "No, none. I feel a lot more energetic. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.06,
      "end_seconds": 118.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "Are you taking anything at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.82,
      "end_seconds": 128.46,
      "duration_seconds": 9.64,
      "text": "A vitamin D tablet, 1000 units, once a day. And an iron tablet last year, but I've stopped."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.84,
      "end_seconds": 131.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.73,
      "text": "Any other conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 133.8,
      "end_seconds": 138.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "An underactive thyroid, and a bit of eczema."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.64,
      "end_seconds": 143.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "Do you drink alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.02,
      "end_seconds": 151.66,
      "duration_seconds": 5.64,
      "text": "Cider, or wine, at weekends. And gluten-free beer, I've discovered."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.71,
      "end_seconds": 175.39,
      "duration_seconds": 4.68,
      "text": "Good. Let me feel your tummy. Lie back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 177.03,
      "end_seconds": 178.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "Okay. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.76,
      "end_seconds": 189.0,
      "duration_seconds": 8.24,
      "text": "Your tummy is soft, no tenderness, and no bloating, and your skin looks healthy, no rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 190.19,
      "end_seconds": 196.4,
      "duration_seconds": 6.21,
      "text": "Her weight's up two kilos since the last visit, doctor. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.45,
      "end_seconds": 215.42,
      "duration_seconds": 17.97,
      "text": "That's good news, Dawn. Kelly, I've got your blood test from last week here. The antibody level has come down a lot, and your iron and vitamin B12 are normal. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 217.4,
      "end_seconds": 220.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "So it's working. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.89,
      "end_seconds": 232.94,
      "duration_seconds": 10.05,
      "text": "Yes, it's responding very well to the diet. I'd say your coeliac disease is well controlled on the gluten-free diet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 235.05,
      "end_seconds": 238.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "Do I need another test? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.63,
      "end_seconds": 256.08,
      "duration_seconds": 15.45,
      "text": "I'd like to repeat the blood test in six months, to make sure the antibody stays down, and I'd like to arrange a bone density check, because coeliac can affect bones."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 257.08,
      "end_seconds": 258.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.42,
      "text": "Okay. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.37,
      "end_seconds": 270.14,
      "duration_seconds": 10.77,
      "text": "Keep the diet strictly, even small amounts of gluten can keep the damage going. And watch cross-contamination, toasters and spreads."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 272.18,
      "end_seconds": 276.62,
      "duration_seconds": 4.44,
      "text": "I've got my own toaster. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.8,
      "end_seconds": 289.2,
      "duration_seconds": 11.4,
      "text": "That's the way. I'd also like you to see the dietitian once a year, and have the flu jab."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 291.24,
      "end_seconds": 293.04,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "Will do. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 294.39,
      "end_seconds": 300.08,
      "duration_seconds": 5.69,
      "text": "I'll book your jab, if you like, Kelly. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 303.04,
      "end_seconds": 305.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "Yes, please. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 307.77,
      "end_seconds": 318.05,
      "duration_seconds": 10.28,
      "text": "If your symptoms come back, or you lose weight, get a rash with blisters, or become very tired, come back sooner."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 319.76,
      "end_seconds": 323.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "I will. Thanks, doctor. Thanks, Dawn. ~"
    }
  ]
}
